this afternoon we get to meet a little  goat that needs a forever home  his name is boozy he was found running  around the streets of downtown las vegas  this past weekend  he was scared as you can imagine but now  he is doing just fine  hector mejia live at the animal  foundation  where boozy is being cared for right now  i think i see him behind you  hey hector yeah so no one cleaned the  goat so now it's up  and available for adoption allow me to  introduce you to  boozy there he is right there he has a  minor cold right now but he's otherwise  in great health  you know he's been the talk of the town  over the past few days and  he is a little shy but he's very nice  and we now know that the male goat is  believed to be about a year and a half  old this past saturday boozy was spotted  running around the streets of downtown  las vegas some actually thought it was a  ram  well metro police and animal control  came in to try and corral him but  i'm told he gave them a hard time they  finally caught him near  umc on charleston just west of rancho  boozy is now getting the best care here  at the animal foundation  but he needs a permanent home dr joe  jared tells me his future owner needs to  keep in mind  that goats are known to be great escape  artists  they always escape so a goat escaping is  not a big deal  a goat escaping i guess in downtown is  kind of unique  again it just reinforces that you have  to have the right  set up or they will find a way out and  then if they're super scared they're  just going to keep running away  so an ideal home would be a barn type  area with running space  he's shy so he needs someone who will  take the time to make him feel  comfortable with people and other pets  the adoption fee is fifty dollars  the animal foundation says this is a  good example of the  wide variety of animals you can find  here for adoption  many automatically think that this place  is just for dogs and cats  reporting from the animal foundation  hector m